In article <4bptio$e2p@nova.avid.com> douglas_thurlow@avid.com (Douglas Thurlow) writes:

>I am trying to put a Seagate Barracuda ST-15150 drive on a DS5000/133 
>running Ultrix 4.4.  But newfs bails out before it's finished.   I 
>edited /etc/disktab to adjust the parameters there for an rz29 drive for 
>the ST15150.  Obviously, this doesn't work too well.

>Does anyone know a better way to do this?  Can it be done?  Can you 
>suggest a disktab entry that would work, or the parameters to newfs to 
>initialize an ST15150?

>Any help would be greatly appreciated.

I have successfully (so far) installed a Seagate ST-15150N to our
DECsystem 5000/240 running Ultrix 4.4.  A friendly DEC person
answered my plea for help in this same Newsgroup.  His advice
was:  1) complete physical installation; secure drive, connect
         cables, set SCSI ID, etc. (ours is in as SZ12 expansion
         box)
      2) use console command "cnfg" to verify drive is recognized
      3) boot system & watch that drive is listed, note device
         name (rz??)
      4) create special device files
          # cd /dev
          # MADEDEV rz??
      5) create small file system (will overwrite it later after
         partioning drive)
          # newfs /dev/rrz??a seagate
         Don't worry about disktab info, Ultrix can get what it
         needs from driver
      6) Plan & partition drive (max partition = 2GB, an Ultrix
         limit) [this was the hard part, tried several times until
         I got it the way I wanted, two 2GB partitions]
           use  /etc/chpt
      7) create file system for each partition
      8) mount & go (edit fstab to include new drive so will mount
         on autoboot)

This is a somewhat abbreviated version of the instructions I was 
given, it not clear, contact me directly.

