The XLs look like a pretty good deal to me. A 233 MHz system with 32MB 
memory, 1GB disk, CDROM, sound card, graphics, 15" color monitor and 
keyboard goes for $6,209. A similarly-configured 100 MHz AlphaStation is 
$6,689. On a cost per SPECint basis, the AlphaStation costs more than 
twice as much as the Alpha XL.

When comparing 233 Mhz systems, the Alpha XL comes in at $6,209 while an 
equivalent AlphaStation 200 4/233 costs $11,785.

When comparing 266 MHz systems, the Alpha XL is $6,809 and the equivalent 
AlphaStation 200 4/266 is $14,700.

The price delta between the 233 MHz and 266 MHz Alpha XLs is $600. The 
price delta between 233 MHz and 266 MHz AlphaStations is $2,915.

The only drawback to the XL is that it is constrained by a 64-bit 
internal bus. 


