king@magrathea.clas.suffolk.edu (Robert King) writes:

| Chris Morgan (chris.morgan@baesema.co.uk) wrote:
| :   How good is Linux on Alpha?
|
| IMHO, Linux on any system is garbage. I would look into NetBSD/alpha.
| It's not an official release yet but it is very workable.

Don't say stuff like that without backing it up with proper reasoning,
please...  I prefer NetBSD to Linux, too, but I don't think that's any
reason to belittle the efforts of Linus Torvalds and his following!

Chris:  You would probably want to look into both of Linux/Alpha and
NetBSD/Alpha, as both are working but unfinished ports.  Ideally, you
should try running both, so that you could compare them.  However, if
it makes a difference to you, Linux is more SVR4ish while NetBSD is,
of course, BSD.  NetBSD also runs on quite a few more hardware
platforms than does Linux, which might be an argument if you see a
multiplatform environment in your future, and would like to run
similar systems.

Info on NetBSD is at "http://www.netbsd.org/".

-tih



