Stephen Hoffman (hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com) wrote:
:   "First-epoch" VAX systems such as the VAX-11/750 are big, old, 
:   power-hungry, and slow.

True.  But for some of us, those are their most endearing qualities!  ;)

Second (?) epoch VAX systems, such as the uVAX II (or VAXstation
II/GPX) in a BA123 enclosure make very nice home systems.  The BA123 is
a good bit smaller than a two-drawer file cabinet, and has space for
five full-height within.  These machines (which run on ordinary
household current) aren't nearly as power hungry as their older
predecessors, they are fairly plentiful in the "you can have it if you
come and get it" market, and they run NetBSD/vax!  Not especially
speedy machines, but quite a bit faster than the rather glacial 11/750.  

