jcp@werple.net.au (John Peterson) wrote:
>I have just inherited a surplus VaxStation 3100, which is short a disk 
>drive. Are there any gotcha's in installing 3rd party SCSI drives 
>(Quantum, Connor etc) in these?  At this stage I would be looking at a 
>1Gb drive + running VAX/VMS 5.5
>
>Thanks in advance
>john
>

You shouldn't use harddisk bigger than 1 Gb. The boot program in 
rom doesn't recognize bigger disks.
My VS3100 runs on a Fujitsu 1606S fast-scsi-2 drive of 1.089 Gb.
There is a problem in VMS 5.5-2 with the scsi implementation of 
ARRE and ARWE bits. VMS 6.2 should run fine, as it does on my VS.
 




