The problem is that the first save set on the tape is the kit install 
save set that is used for the upgrade procedures.  It doesn't have any 
disk format info (or anything else useful for a scartch install for that 
matter).  You will need to specify the name of the saveset to restore.


Unfortunately, I don't have the old documentation with me and I don't 
remember exactly how the save set was specified in VMS 5.2.  I THINK the 
saveset was called "REQUIRED", but it may have been VMS052.B.  You can 
try either of the 2 filenames.  If the saveset is not found you will have 
to either get a directory of the tape or wait for someone with the old 
documentation to reply.  

The backup command will be something like:

$ backup/verify mua0:required/save dua0:

You will also need to get the license PAKs installed.  If I remember 
right, DECwindows wouldn't allow a login unless a valid VMS license was 
loaded.


