In article <4ap4biINN5mt@dur-news.ctron.com>, poisson@ctron.com (Matt Poisson) writes...
>Hi.  I have a couple of questions concerning the DEC GigaSwitch.
> 
>1)  Does anyone know how to force the ports to go into full-duplex mode?  I 
>    would like to do some testing and it requires putting the ports into
>    full-duplex.  I have looked at the mibs and the OBM session and cannot
>    find anything.
> 
>2)  With regards to the FGL4 line card, how do you or can you change the ports
>    to be "S" ports.  I don't have any documentation on the line card.  I
>    know you can do it to the FGL2 but wasn't sure if you could with these.
> 

    No, you can't force the cards into full duplex.  They are enabled for full
duplex by default and will enter it if the other partner supports full duplex
and is enabled for it.

    There are three MIB objects of interest in the DEC ELAN MIB:

    eFDXEnable   ...tells you if FFDT (full duplex) is enabled on the port

    eFDXOp       ...tells you if it's operating in full duplex or not

    eFDXState    ...tells you the full duplex state

     ...for your second question - all FGL-4 ports come up as "S" type ports by
default.  You can only change them to "M" type ports - this is done with SNMP -
look for the mPortEnable object in the GIGAswitch MIB.

...have fun

MDL



