organization: Canadian Institute for Theoretical Astrophysics
reply-to: mark@cita.toronto.edu
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

[ Jeff Scheib ]

| Any utilities out there which can warn of pending license PAK expiration for
| OSF/1?  

Well, it's rather trivial to use existing tools.  It took less than five minutes
to cook up the following shell script; some minor variant of it could be invoked
by cron on the first day of each month ...

---------------

#!/bin/sh

set `date`
mon_year=`echo $2-$6|tr '[a-z]' '[A-Z]'`

paklist=`
	lmf list full |
	egrep 'Product Name:|Key Termination Date:' |
	sed 's/.*: *//' |
	awk '	(NR%2) == 1		{ prodname = $1 }
		(NR%2) == 0 && NF != 0	{ termdate = $1; printf "%11s %s\n", termdate, prodname } ' |
	sed 's/...//' |
	awk '	$1 == "'$mon_year'"	{ print $2 }'
`

if test -n "$paklist"; then
	echo "The following PAKs expire this month:

$paklist" | Mail -s "PAK expiry alert!" your_sysadmin
fi

---------------

