written.  The Alpha is a 64/32 bit CPU.  Well, more important for this,
it can only do 32bit and 64bit memory cycles.  If you want to read/write
a bit, byte, or 16bit word, you have to load 32 or 64 bits into a register,
read/modify it there.

If the compiler can figure it out, there are instructions to do multiple
operations on a 64bit register.

For doing 32bit or 64bit operations, the alpha will likely be much faster.
Especially, I might hope, floating point.

But for 8 or 16bit operations, maybe not.

-- glen



