Subhash Jawahrani (sjawahra@us.oracle.com) wrote:
: $ ftp dmcalpha1
: Connected to dmcalpha1.us.oracle.com.
: 220 dmcalpha1 FTP server (OSF/1 Version 5.60) ready.
: Name (dmcalpha1:root): anonymous


: ftp> ls
: 200 PORT command successful.
: 150 Opening ASCII mode data connection for /bin/ls (dmsiris2,2242).
: /bin/ls: No such file or directory
: 226 Transfer complete.
: ftp> 

: What can be the problem.


The anonymous ftp does a "chroot" (for supposed security reasons).  This
makes the /usr/spool/ftp (or whereever the "ftp" account has it's home
directory) appear to be the root of the filesystem for the server
process.  You therefore need to simulate soe of the stuff that you
would normally have on the root disk.  Most importantly "/bin/ls"
needs to be there for the directory list operations.  Just copy
/bin/ls to /usr/spool/ftp/bin/ls...

-Ron



