We have scattered reports of this and other floppy related behaviors with
the 2.1 setup.

If you cannot or don't wish to exchange this kit for a CD kit, here's what you
can do to work around this problem:

Copy the floppies to the hard disk or network share and install from there. 
Here's how:

  Place the first diskette into the drive and look at a:\common\diskette.inf. 
    This file contains a good list of the disk names of all the floppies, 
    right near the top of the file. Note that the end of each line makes a
    relative directory reference, like: ..\DISK1I 

  Create a temporary directory on your hard disk or network drive and then 
    create subdirectories for each of the disks listed in the diskette.inf file. 
  Now use xcopy /s or use Windows file manager or Windows 95 explorer to copy 
    the files and directories on all of the eXcursion floppies into the 
    directories you created above. 

  Once the copying is complete, run the setup.exe in the DISK1I subdirectory 
    and eXcursion should install in a matter of minutes. 

#Gary

