Performance is about 3.8 VUP (1 VUP = 11/780 speed) for a 3100/38, you can run
either VMS (make sure you get the licences with the machine though :-) later
than 5.3 (I think) or Ultrix.. something that DEC likes to forget about :-(
a BSD 4.3 UNIX with added DEC bits. Typical uses are as X Terminals or perhaps
a reasonably powered standalone system. I'm not sure relative to an x86 as
this isn't a fair question. The whole system should be taken into
consideration.
However running X with a 16mb system seems to me appreciably faster and more
stable than say eXceed on a 486DX2-66 or even a P75. I guess its a case of
horse for courses as they say. A straightforward 3100 though is a bit slower
than a model 38. I'd go the the 38's all things considered equal...

How much memory have these systems? What size SCSI drives? What are they
currently used for? they are nice machines, I upgraded my VAXstation-2000
(0.9 VUP!) to one. 

