In article <4b1tph$4d9@cc-server9.massey.ac.nz>, R.Faber@massey.ac.nz writes:
>So, my LN03 decided to quit working, I had a good look around for some info 
>but my search didn't turn up very much.  Any suggestions where I might find 
>some info online?
>
>Failing that instead of calling the blinking little man, what does the error 
>code 2  mean?

The little man and the number 2 says that there is an optical system error. 
That is, the printer doesn't see the sync pulse from the laser scanner.  There
are a variety of causes for this, including:

	- bad print engine drive board
	- bad laser scanner board
	- bad laser
	- bad power supply

But, the most common problem is that the +24v isn't being passed by some
interlock.

On the side door, and on the development drawer are a couple of pins that, when
the door/drawer are closed, connect to a socket inside the printer.  The 24v
that runs the main motor and the laser scanner passes through these
pin/sockets, forming an interlock.  The problem is usually due to the ends of
the pins being pitted or corroded, since everytime you open the door, you get a
little arc as the connection is broken.  Try looking at, and if needed,
cleaning these connections.

