> ??
> 
> I know it's doing hardware diagnostics when you power it up, but what
> I don't know is which subsystems are failing (1 and 0). Can anyone tell
> me which subsystems are failing?
> 

From the manual.

Test Code	Component Tested	Action to Take if Subtest Fails
----------------------------------------------------------------
7			Video SIM module	Contact Digital Service
6			VDAC and PCC		Contact Digital Service
5			DZ serial line		Contact Digital Service
4			Systems Module		Follow SCSI Troubleshooting (chap. 6).
3			Keyboard and Mouse	Follow Keyboard/mouse Troubleshooting (chap6)
2			Network I/F (LANCE)	Follow Ethernet Troubleshooting (chap 6.)
1			Disks & SCSI		Contact Digital Service
0			End of test			Successful completion

The last number displayed is the test that failed. Since it was 2 you have
a network problem of some sort. 

Is your hardware plugged into the network?
If so, is the proper port selected with switch in back (AUI or 10B2)?
The selected port will have a green LED lit next to it.
If no network connection is there a loopback connector on the selected port?

The test for the network I/F sends out a data and expects to read it back. A
'good' network connection or a loopback connector will fullfill this 
requirement.

