>From a C program running on either a VAX/VMS or an ALPHA/VMS, I'd 
like
>to read the first 16Kbytes of some files.  Some of the files exist 
on
>a Sun/Sparc and some exist on another VAX/VMS system.  All 
accesses
>are done via DECNET.  The program is able to open the data files 
>on either system.
<snip>
>I also tried to access the file from DCL.  I was able to open it 
>(open/share/read), but was not able to read data from the file.
>
>Suggestions?
>Has anybody had success in reading SUN files across DECNET?
>
>Ray Muzic
>rfm2@po.cwru.edu

If you get the following, I can show you how to fix it:
 $ Open/share/read       file remote::file.dat
 $ read/nolock/end=close file record
%RMS-F-BUFSIZ, 644 byte record is too big for users buffer.

Fix:
 $ SET RMS_DEFAULT/NETWORK=24 	!the default is 3, Max is 24.
 $                              !I got this info from DEC support.
 $ Open/share/read       file remote::file.dat
 $ read/nolock/end=close file record
 $ !success


========================================
Steve Sparrow @ Computer Sciences Corporation




