In article <alherb-1412951635400001@alherb.digex.net>, alherb@access.digex.net 
says...
>
>Does anyone know if it's possible to add a PCMCIA slot to an Alpha 2100 
server?

For hardware, there exist some ISA or PCI cards that will provide 1 or 2 
PCMCIA cards slots.

You'll also need software support in the form of PCMCIA card and socket 
services, plus device drivers.  Currently, both Digital Unix and OpenVMS both 
do not have any software support for the PCMCIA bus.  Intel Linux has some 
support for the PCMCIA bus, but I don't know if it has been ported to the 
Alpha version, or even if there is a Alpha Linux version that runs on the 
2100.

The PCMCIA bus is under consideration for support in future releases of both 
Digital Unix and OpenVMS.  I cannot provide any time frame for this support, 
only that PCMCIA support is on the list for the future.


