I am currently restoring a PDP-11 based music synthesizer
called the "McLeyvier", after its designer, David McLey.
It is based on a PDP-11/23 running RSX-11M v3.2.

Unfortunately, the disk controller is non-DEC (DTC 520-1)
and it only speaks to ST-506 and ST-412 drives.   Also,
it uses a Peritek VRG-Q video display.   This means that RSX
has been extensively patched, but the sources are long
gone.

Since I want to upgrade the disks to something more modern,
I will have to also upgrade to a newer version of RSX.
This means that I will have to compare the current
RSX11M.TSK file with a virgin v3.2 system and figure
out the differences.   Likewise with the half-duplex
terminal driver.   Then I will make the same changes
to a v4.x system.

The system is housed in the sort of roll-around cases
that you see used in road shows.   There is about 4"
of padding between the inner and outer walls.

I would like to correspond with anyone who has any memory
of the McLeyvier.

