If you're using the same VM structure as Digital Unix, VMS or NT, you
can probably (and should probably) use existing palcode.

While David Mazieres was an intern at DEC-WRL, he wrote a "palcode
disassembler". We converted it into a loadable device driver and
improved security a little. Basically, it lets you disassemble the
existing palcode on a running machine, modify it (using a symbolic
assembler) and then drop it back into the PALcode area on that machine.

This has been very useful for e.g., low-cost TLB instrumentation.

If you want this version, let me know.


