Y'know, about 200 million years ago when we were still using things like
7-track 200 bpi tapes, the problems of exchanging data on tapes was already
there.

And y'know what else ?

People actually came up with a standard (or "universal format" as you call it),
and, lo, the standard was to be known as ANSI-standard labelled tapes.

And furthermore, the standard was adopted by all creeds and races, and,
yea, as unto one, the standard was a successful one.  MVS could talk to
Multics, who could talk unto VMS, who could talk unto GEORGE (ICL), who
could talk unto CDC NOS, who could talk unto Burroughs CANDE, and, verily,
the world was as one.

And then ... came UNIX (well, actually I know it predates VMS, and it
shows ! :-) ...

And here endeth the lesson for today.

