Well Lightwave 3D is 3d renderer and modeller used for video effects in such 
shows as Babylon 5, VR5, Earth2, Robocop the TV show and loads of other 
productions. 

When you are doing a comparison like this you have to take into account the OS
as well, it would have been better if they had both been done under NT, as
don't forget W95 has so much hand coded INTEL assembler in that its totally
unportable to other uProcessors and will give a perfomance boost to the Intel
box (thats why W95 will never appear on Alpha/PowerPC/Sparc).

So for the ideal comparison we should have the following:

PCI motherboards, same HDs, same HD controller, same CD-Rom drive, Matrox 
Millenium Graphics card with 8MB Wram, 32 MB RAM, .5MB Secondary Cache, Latest
version of WinNT, latest version of LightWave 3D. Then once all external 
differences have been eliminated we can have a real head to head. Somehow I
imagine that the 10 second difference can be accounted for by I/O differences,
but I stand to be corrected by anyone who has done this type of test. One last
thing we need to know whether LightWave has been compiled with any specialist
optimisations for each processor, and which bits if any are handcoded asm.

