frederic_bouquet@ascus.com (Fred) wrote:
>We receive the following error message when we try to connect to Rdb
>database on VMS using an ODBC driver :
>
>[DEC] [ODBC] [rdb] %SQLSRV - FTEXEERR,fatal execute server error
>%SYSTEM_F_NOPRIV,insufficient privilege or object protection violation
>
>This kind of message is so 'guru friendly' that I can't understand it.
>Any help would be appreciated
>
>
>============================================
>Frederic Bouquet, frederic_bouquet@ascus.com
>============================================

The NOPRIV part of the message is what gives you the clue to the problem.
It's telling you that you don't have priviledge to access one or more of 
the files or directories.  To test this, you could run the program from 
the SYSTEM or other priviledged account.  The error should no longer 
occur.   

You need to check the protection on the files to make sure the intended 
account has read and execute access to all the images and read and write 
access to all data files.  You should also check the directory files for
at least read access and possibly read/write access by the user.

Note: I am not an RDB or ODBC expert.  The above info is based on the 
messages you displayed.

