I'm not quite sure why you're surprised. 

I don't know what lightwave 3D is, and you don't say whether the application
that you were running was compiled for Alpha NT.  Assuming that it was, these
results still don't surprise me at all.  The 166MHz chip used in the AXPpci33 is at
 the bottom end of the Alpha range and has been around for nearly 2 years now.
133MHz Pentium is a fairly new development and is still pretty much state of the 
art.  A fairer comparison would be with a state-of the art Alpha design such as 
the 21164/300 .

Also, you have ignored any i/o card restrictions which could affect the
performance of this test e.g. disk/graphics performance.

In its defence, the Alpha 166MHz can run a 64bit OS ( Digital UNIX ) - 
something the Pentium 133 will never do !     

