Windows NT which
> will allow Windows NT/Alpha to run 32-bit Windows NT/Intel applications.
> 
>

WOW (Windows on Windows?) is embedded in NT on Alpha. It will emulate 286 code.

FX!32 is to permit the translation of 32bit Win95  Intel binaries to Alpha
binaries.

Applications using 386 unique instructions (i.e., a driver) are
accommodated by SoftWindows and SoftPC.....neither of which is available
for Alpha running NT at this time....but an implied announcement was made
in the 11/6/95 Press release on FX!32 by DEC's VP Caldwell.

