In <Geert.Deleu-0312952200280001@dialup20.roeselare.eunet.be> Geert.Deleu@ping.be (Geert Deleu) writes:

>I have looked at alpha 21064a 275mhz proc and P133.
>Looking a some specs i can no see he difference anymore in performance!
>I am I wrong, or is this true?

Look again:

System            CPU        ClkMHz  Cache      SPECint SPECfp  Info  Source
Name              (NUMx)Type ext/in  Ext+I/D      92      92    Date  Obtained
================= ========== ======= ========== ======= ======= ===== =========
Dell DimensionXPS Pentium    66/133  512+8/8     177.9   116.0  Nov95 www.intel
DEC 2[01]00/4/275 A21064A    39/275  4M+16/16    202.9   292.6  Apr95 Digital

Can you see a difference in performance?  Note that the performance
data for the Pentium system are obtained in a Microsoft-free environment:
UnixWare plus the Intel reference compilers.  Don't expect to see
something similar from Borland C++ or Microsoft PowerStation Fortran.

OTOH, if you're shopping for an NT box to run commercial software, the
Dell system mentioned above has a slightly better SYSmark/NT than an
AlphaStation 250 4/266 (and it is a lot cheaper :-)

>also averybody tells me: buy a 21164, but the price difference 
>between the 21064a and 21164 is hughe,... I can no get that...

Then, don't buy a 21164.

Without knowing what you need the machine for, it's impossible to advise
one way or another.

Dan
