Although possible, I haven't seen any permanent damage from hooking up
the wrong monitors...
What are you hooking them too? If an Alpha, at least you need to have
the proper connector. From there, it would need to be able to sync up.
The horizontal and vertical scans must meet the needs of the card.
Most of the Alpha cards require standard VGA and up. The monitor must
do a 31.5 KHz (I think) horizontal scan and go up (higher scan and
resolution) from there.

Hope this helps - STeve




