In article <mpitman-2811952224440001@ubppp-00.ppp-net.buffalo.edu>, mpitman@acsu.buffalo.edu writes:
:I have a VAXCluster with a VaxServer 3300 & a Vaxstation 3100m38 running
:VMS 5.4-1.
:Can I connect a Laserjet to this cluster? It seems the sysyem software
:supports only DEC printers. Can anyone help??

  Digital's DCPS-Open package supports various HP LaserJet printers.
  DECdirect (an interactive version of the catalog is available at
  http://www.digital.com) has information on this particular package.

  You will want to check with the system adminstration folks about
  the license and package availability -- I don't know what sort of
  licenses (CSLG, NAS, etc) your site has, nor what sort of software
  distribution is available at your site.

  You will (obviously) need a serial port.  (I do not recommend using
  the console line for this purpose -- the VAXstation 3100 has a
  serial port intended for a printer.)

