were named 4/190, 4/233 and so on. This, however, had NOTHING to do wit the 
4 processor capability of the machine, but only told you that it was using 
EV4 (21064/A) processors. Now you can upgrade a DECserver 2100 4/xxx to a
5/xxx by replacing the EV4 with EV5 (21164) processors. We have re-used the 
cingle CPU from on of our two main servers in the other (thus upgrading 
that machine form a single-CPU DECserver 2100 4/266 to a two cpu  2100 4/266)
and got two new 5/250 cpu's for the other 2100, thus upgrading this one to a
2100 5/250 with 2 cpus.

So, in fact, it IS easy, you're just mislead by the accidental coincidence of 
a maximum of 4 cpus in the 2100 and the use of EV4 cpus in the first generation...

Uwe



